  ],
  "confidence": "verified",
  "notes": [
    "Needs two supplies: VDD 3-5.5 V logic and VMOT 8-35 V motor. Both grounds go to the common ground.",
    "RESET is floating: connect it to SLEEP (or HIGH). SLEEP is pulled up on Pololu boards; some clones leave it floating.",
    "Set the current limit before connecting the motor (Vref = 8 x I x Rsense; Rsense is 0.068 Ohm on Pololu boards, often 0.1 Ohm on clones).",
    "Never connect or disconnect the motor while powered.",
    "Put a 47-100 uF electrolytic capacitor across VMOT/GND close to the board.",
    "About 1 A per coil without a heatsink; up to 2 A per coil only with good cooling."
  ],
